  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "My Shark cordless battery got really hot on charge last night and this morning it looks puffed up, the plastic case has split at the seam a bit. Can I still use it till a new one comes? It's the IZ201UK."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nA swollen, very hot or chemical-smelling battery can catch fire. Stop using and charging it now, unplug the charger, and if it is safe to move put it somewhere non-flammable away from anything that could burn. Don't puncture, squeeze or try to open the battery, and don't put it in the household bin — take it to a battery recycling point. No, you must not use the vacuum or continue charging this battery. A swollen and overheating lithium-ion battery poses an immediate fire risk and could fail catastrophically. From what you have checked, this needs an appliance engineer to look at it: the next steps are beyond the checks that are safe to do yourself."
  }
